command: fixed_items CHANGELOG.md (the "Fixed" items citing specs/0045-publish.md):
    - An of-pie plot with no split: no `splitType` element is written, the schema's default being `auto`, where `auto` was written and Excel refused the chart (`specs/0045-publish.md`, fix 1; `records/excel-check-m7-2026-10-26.md`).
    - A workbook element the rewrite creates, `workbookProtection`, `definedNames` or `calcPr`: it goes immediately before the next main-namespace child in schema order, or before the root's end tag, so an element of another namespace that Excel wrote after `workbookPr` stays before it, where the created element went before that one and Excel refused the order (`specs/0045-publish.md`, fix 2, decision 1 A; `records/excel-check-m7-2026-10-26.md`).
    - A new scatter plot of `ScatterStyle::None`: `add_chart` and `add_chartsheet` refuse it, "a new scatter plot takes a scatter style other than none", where the style was written and Excel refused it; the reader keeps `None` (`specs/0045-publish.md`, fix 3, decision 2 A; `records/excel-check-m7-2026-10-26.md`).
    - A chartsheet's only chart: a write that would leave a chartsheet's drawing with no chart frame is refused, "a chartsheet keeps its chart", where the empty drawing was written and Excel refused it; a removal and an addition in one write replace the chart (`specs/0045-publish.md`, fix 4; `records/excel-check-m7-2026-10-26.md`).
