command: the doc comment's second and third paragraphs, joined:
    emend is a pure-Rust library for read-modify-write of Office Open XML spreadsheets: open an 
    existing .xlsx, change what you were asked to change, hand the file back with everything else 
    intact. It parses only what an edit touches and passes every other zip entry through byte for byte. 
    The comparison point is openpyxl, and the definition is exact: like openpyxl, emend does not 
    evaluate formulas (it stores formula strings and reads cached values), does not render, does not 
    autofit, and does not fix up references on row or column insertion. Those limits are by design and 
    are not gaps. 
